            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0864" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/380: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-28T14:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 28—8:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>431. Your 251, October 26, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d525-f1"/> Norwegian Minister has stated that he is unable to join
                    in identic telegram as he believes that his Government has not adhered to arms
                    embargo resolution of Washington Conference and consequently is not acquainted
                    with details of matter (see my despatch no. 1033, October 14<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d525-f2"/>). No further development in status of arms embargo
                    agreement has occurred and Netherlands Minister still maintains position already
                    taken. Matter will come up for discussion again at meeting of diplomatic body in
                    near future.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
